\section{Final Reflections}

This project demonstrates that the intersection of geographic information systems, transportation engineering, and autonomous vehicle technology creates powerful opportunities for innovation. By bridging the gap between real-world complexity and simulation requirements, we enable more effective development and deployment of autonomous vehicle technologies that will ultimately improve transportation safety, efficiency, and sustainability.

The successful implementation of comprehensive Istanbul district models proves that automated generation of professional-quality simulation environments is not only feasible but essential for the scalable development of autonomous vehicle systems. As urban environments continue to evolve and autonomous vehicle technology advances, tools like this system will become increasingly critical for ensuring safe, reliable, and effective transportation solutions.

The future of transportation simulation lies in the seamless integration of real-world complexity with virtual testing environments, and this project establishes a foundation for that integration while demonstrating its practical value through real-world application to one of the world's most challenging urban transportation networks.

